  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "9664e658b3df1c5ae7d466af9d73bc0eb1dbabb2",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 972782930,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Not really related, but should these fields be FT_UINT32 ?\n\n\n./tools/check_typed_item_calls.py --file epan/dissectors/packet-woww.c\n\nExamining:\n\nepan/dissectors/packet-woww.c \n\n\n\nWarning: epan/dissectors/packet-woww.c:4745 ptvcursor_add called for hf_woww_character_race  -  item type is FT_UINT8 but call has len 4\n\nWarning: epan/dissectors/packet-woww.c:4746 ptvcursor_add called for hf_woww_character_gender  -  item type is FT_UINT8 but call has len 4\n\nWarning: epan/dissectors/packet-woww.c:4747 ptvcursor_add called for hf_woww_character_class  -  item type is FT_UINT8 but call has len 4\n\n3 warnings",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-06-06T16:47:20.119Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-06-06T18:05:09.988Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 158836572,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 279822,
            "username": "alagoutte",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Alexis La Goutte",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a15cba6417f4d1723eb56add7099bcfd8df373dc520577958b33c37915ef231b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/alagoutte"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2022-06-14T05:41:11.359Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 7075,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 972866863,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I'm not sure. The field and logical element (race/gender/class) is a `FT_UINT8` and it's sent this way in other messages, but in this instance it is sent as a `FT_UINT32`. It's an artifact of the protocol not really being designed but at times just being structs serialized directly onto the network without people really paying attention.\n\nI guess an option would be to add it as an `FT_UINT8` no matter what \"real\" size it is and then just skip the 3 \"padding\" bytes, or would that be weird?\n\nSo doing something like\n```c\nptvcursor_add(ptv, hf_woww_character_race, 1, ENC_NA);\nptvcursor_advance(ptv, 3); // hf_woww_character_race is sent with padding\nptvcursor_add(ptv, hf_woww_character_gender, 1, ENC_NA);\nptvcursor_advance(ptv, 3); // hf_woww_character_gender is sent with padding\nptvcursor_add(ptv, hf_woww_character_class, 1, ENC_NA);\nptvcursor_advance(ptv, 3); // hf_woww_character_class is sent with padding\n```\n\n\nAlso, just saw that you actually mentioned this almost a year ago. Sorry about not responding, I've been really busy. :/",
          "author": {
            "id": 8833908,
            "username": "gtker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "gtker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/aa4c12e53ad3f19de87a734aecc1ae8300e79561705147e9ff0c56eb1393ee28?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/gtker"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-06-06T18:05:09.817Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-06-06T18:05:09.817Z",
